Model 1 (Ayn/SmolLM):
The decision is based upon the following legal principles:

1. The law should be applied to all cases;
2. The law must not discriminate against any person or group by providing a different set of rules for different groups/classes of people;
3. The law cannot provide an exception that would allow one class of persons to have access only to certain types of information while others are denied access altogether;
4. The law does not give special privileges to some classes over other classes without giving them equal rights under it;
5. The law requires courts to apply their own standards when deciding whether there has been discrimination between two parties because they may differ from each other’s standard of conduct as laid down in the applicable law;
6. The law provides no remedy if such discrimination occurs
